<title>CANADA: Redaurum wins Botswana diamond search deal.</title>
<headline>Redaurum wins Botswana diamond search deal.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Redaurum Ltd said on Tuesday it had acquired exclusive diamond prospecting rights on a property in Botswana.</p>
<p>The 962.5 square km area in the Central District of Botswana is right next to De Beers Consolidated Mines Ltd's Orapa diamond mine, Redaurum said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the ground is regarded as highly prospective for the discovery of diamond-bearing kimberlite and deposits of alluvial diamonds that may have eroded and transported from the large Orapa and Letlhakane cluster of kimberlite pipes.</p>
<p>	  -- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
